  - web security
abstract: >-
  APIShield is a real-time, hybrid machine-learning security gateway that detects and blocks
  seven API attack types (SQL injection, parameter tampering, brute force, credential stuffing,
  broken object level authorization, API flooding and token replay) by jointly analysing request
  payload features and causal behavioural features over per-IP and per-token sliding windows.
  The repository includes the gateway, a vulnerable test API, a traffic generator, the machine-learning
  pipeline, a labelled eight-class dataset (11,415 requests), validation notebooks, and a ModSecurity
  baseline comparison.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22143601"
